   "text": {
    "L1": "To compare decimals, start at the left and compare the whole parts.",
    "L2": "If those match, compare tenths, then hundredths, moving place by place.",
    "L3": "A longer decimal is not automatically bigger. For example, 0.5 is bigger than 0.125.",
    "L4": "Write zeros at the end when useful: 0.5 becomes 0.500, and 0.45 becomes 0.450.",
    "L5": "In the worked example, 0.500 is largest because its tenths digit is 5, while the others have 4.",
    "L6": "Between the two numbers with 4 tenths, compare hundredths: 0.450 is bigger than 0.405.",
    "L7": "So the order is 0.405, then 0.45, then 0.5.",
    "L8": "There are more decimals between two decimals. Between 0.2 and 0.3, 0.27 is seven small steps after 0.2.",
    "L9": "Now order these decimals from smallest to biggest."
   },
